From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMCX <noreply@openmcx.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] presence: the NOTIFYs of a subscription leave in CSeq order

RFC 3261 clause 12.2.1.1: the CSeq of a request within a dialog "MUST be
strictly monotonically increasing"; clause 12.2.2: a UAS answers a request
with a lower CSeq than the last one received with a 500. notify() took the
next CSeq of the subscription under the lock of its hash slot, released it,
and then built and sent the NOTIFY: the first NOTIFY of a reg event
subscription, whose body is built from the presentity table, left after the
NOTIFY that a PUBLISH of the same registration made in another process with
its body ready, and the UE answered the first one 500. A reentrant lock per
hash slot (the reply callback may run in the same process) is now held from
taking the CSeq to sending the request.

---
